<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malays</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Malay people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Malays are an Austronesian people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, the coasts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>. Most are Muslims, and Malay culture took shape in sultanates such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a>, whose language became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lingua-franca">lingua franca</a> of maritime South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. They form the majority population of Malaysia and Brunei.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malays.jpg" alt="Malays" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Orhanghazi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Malay_tricolour.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
